  "raw_text": "Yes. `git reset --hard` discards uncommitted changes to **tracked files** in both the working tree and staging area, resetting them to the target commit (default: `HEAD`).\n\n```bash\ngit reset --hard HEAD\n```\n\nThis generally does **not** remove untracked files; use `git clean` for those. Discarded tracked-file edits can be difficult or impossible to recover, so consider `git stash` first.",
